== Title decisions ==

* '''[[Token]] → [[Token (blockchain)]]''' because “token” is heavily overloaded across authentication, programming, language modeling, economics, and physical objects.
* '''[[Oracle]] → [[Oracle (blockchain)]]''' because oracle has durable meanings in databases, logic, computation, religion, and ordinary language.
* [[Attestation]] remains unqualified because the Core page deliberately covers the general digital/evidentiary assertion concept and then links blockchain/credential applications.
* [[Hash function]], [[Arbitrage]], [[Slippage]], and [[Price impact]] remain broad public concepts rather than blockchain-specific aliases.
* [[Concentrated liquidity]] remains a generic mechanism; Uniswap v3 is the historically important implementation/source, not the definition.
* [[Decentralized identity]] is broader than W3C DID and is not defined as “identity on a blockchain.”

== Scope exclusions ==

The wave deliberately excludes protocol-specific routers, hooks, vault standards, token standards, fee mechanisms, and named product architectures unless they independently justify public canonical concepts.

ERC-4626, reCLAMM, Uniswap routers/hooks, Balancer routers/hooks, and project-specific tokenomics remain examples or future scoped topics rather than Wave 11 primitives.

== Domain decision ==

No new controlled Domain is introduced. Wave 11 uses:

* Computer science
* Mathematics
* Technology
* Systems science
* Philosophy

